  "question": {
    "text": "<p>For a concrete sphere of radius <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi></math> having a cavity of radius <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi></math> packed with sawdust, to float&nbsp;with its entire volume submerged under water what will be the ratio of mass of concrete to mass of sawdust? Given the specific gravities&nbsp;of concrete and sawdust are respectively <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"> <mrow> <mn>2.4</mn></mrow> </math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"> <mrow> <mn>0.3</mn></mrow> </math>.</p>\r"
  },
